# Redis Presence and Connection Verification Commands
# You can execute these commands in redis-cli (inside the Redis docker container or directly).
# Connection command: docker exec -it chat_redis redis-cli

# 1. List all active presence keys in Redis
KEYS presence:*

# 2. List all active user socket connections
KEYS connections:*

# 3. List socket-to-user mappings
KEYS socket:*

# 4. Check details of a specific user presence key (Replace UUID placeholder)
# GET presence:UUID
# Returns: "online" / "offline" (or value set by realtime-service)

# 5. Check active socket IDs mapped to a specific user (Replace UUID placeholder)
# SMEMBERS connections:UUID
# Returns a list of socket connection IDs for that user

# 6. Verify TTL of a user presence key
# TTL presence:UUID
# If configured as a sliding transient state, this should have a positive TTL (e.g. 60 seconds)
